      "body": "@22quinn would you mind taking a look when you have a minute? One-file fix in default_loader.py, the log said 0.00s whenever the weights iterator was skipped.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-30T18:37:11Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63022#issuecomment-6530674493",
      "id": 6530674493,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-30T18:37:11Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "raghavyadav01"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing this as a duplicate of #37689, which fixes the same bug and was opened first. Sorry I missed it. One difference that might be worth keeping there: starting the timer on entry to `load_weights()` also counts the weight download, which #14063 moved out of this number on purpose. Taking the start time when the iterator is first pulled, with a fallback for the skipped case, keeps that. (AI-assisted.)\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:28:02Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63022#issuecomment-6548092884",
      "id": 6548092884,
